# Pruebas del BFF en tu PC. Requiere la extensión "REST Client" de VS Code (clic en "Send Request" sobre cada bloque).
# Ejecútalas EN ORDEN: la 3 usa el paymentId de la 2, y la 9 usa el pedido de la 3.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8088

### 1. Catálogo -> 200 con los 12 productos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products

### 2. Pago aprobado -> 200 con paymentId, authorizationCode, amount
# @name charge
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [{ "productoId": 7, "cantidad": 1 }],
  "card": { "number": "4242424242424242", "name": "TEST USER", "expiry": "12/29", "cvv": "123" }
}

### 3. Crear pedido con ese pago -> 201 con id y estado CREADO
# @name order
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clienteId": "CLI-123456785",
  "clienteNombre": "Test User",
  "clienteEmail": "test@example.com",
  "clienteDireccion": "Av. Test 123, Santiago",
  "clienteRut": "12.345.678-5",
  "paymentId": "{{charge.response.body.$.paymentId}}",
  "items": [{ "productoId": 7, "cantidad": 1 }]
}

### 4. Reusar el mismo pago -> 409 PAYMENT_USED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clienteId": "CLI-123456785", "clienteNombre": "Test User", "clienteEmail": "test@example.com",
  "clienteDireccion": "Av. Test 123", "clienteRut": "12.345.678-5",
  "paymentId": "{{charge.response.body.$.paymentId}}",
  "items": [{ "productoId": 7, "cantidad": 1 }]
}

### 5. Pedido SIN pago -> 402 PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clienteId": "CLI-1", "clienteNombre": "Test User", "clienteEmail": "test@example.com",
  "clienteDireccion": "Av. Test 123", "clienteRut": "12.345.678-5",
  "items": [{ "productoId": 7, "cantidad": 1 }]
}

### 6. Tarjeta rechazada -> 402 CARD_DECLINED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [{ "productoId": 7, "cantidad": 1 }],
  "card": { "number": "4000000000000002", "name": "TEST USER", "expiry": "12/29", "cvv": "123" }
}

### 7. Sin fondos -> 402 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [{ "productoId": 7, "cantidad": 1 }],
  "card": { "number": "4000000000009995", "name": "TEST USER", "expiry": "12/29", "cvv": "123" }
}

### 8. Más unidades que el stock (el producto 9 tiene 15) -> 409 InvalidStockException
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [{ "productoId": 9, "cantidad": 99 }],
  "card": { "number": "4242424242424242", "name": "TEST USER", "expiry": "12/29", "cvv": "123" }
}

### 9. Precio manipulado: el total del pedido debe ser el del catálogo (14500), NO 1
# @name charge2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [{ "productoId": 7, "cantidad": 1 }],
  "card": { "number": "4242424242424242", "name": "TEST USER", "expiry": "12/29", "cvv": "123" }
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clienteId": "CLI-2", "clienteNombre": "Test User", "clienteEmail": "test@example.com",
  "clienteDireccion": "Av. Test 123", "clienteRut": "12.345.678-5",
  "paymentId": "{{charge2.response.body.$.paymentId}}",
  "items": [{ "productoId": 7, "cantidad": 1, "precioUnitario": 1 }]
}

### 10. Listar pedidos (admin) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders

### 11. Cambiar estado del pedido de la prueba 3 -> 200 (o 409 si la transición no está permitida)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nuevoEstado": "ACEPTADO" }

### 12. Editar stock de un producto (admin) -> 200 con el stock nuevo
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products/7
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stock": 40 }
